## Project at a glance

A static site — **<name / purpose / type>** — built with **Astro** and deployed to **Cloudflare Workers** via the **`@astrojs/cloudflare`** adapter (Workers Static Assets, *not* Cloudflare Pages). Static by default, with the adapter installed so individual pages can become dynamic later.

Live at **https://<canonical-domain>**. Auto-deploys from GitHub on every push to `main` (Cloudflare Workers Builds).

## Commands

| Command | Purpose |
| :--- | :--- |
| `npm run dev` | Astro dev server (workerd) at `localhost:4321`. When an AI agent runs it, Astro backgrounds it and prints the URL — check with `npx astro dev status` / `logs`, stop with `npx astro dev stop` (not Ctrl-C or `pkill`). Don't use `wrangler dev`. |
| `npm run check` | `astro check` type-check. |
| `npm run build` | `astro check && astro build` → `dist/client/` (static assets + the generated `wrangler.json`). `dist/server/` is filled only once a page opts into on-demand rendering. Type errors fail the build, locally and in CI. |
| `npm run preview` | Serves the production build (CSP and `_headers` active). Backgrounds itself under an agent — stop with `npx astro preview stop`. |
| `npm run verify` | `build` + `wrangler deploy --dry-run` — no login, nothing deployed. Expect `0 errors`, `[build] Complete!`, `No bindings found.` |
| `npm run deploy` | `build` + `wrangler deploy` from a laptop. **Pushing to `main` is the primary deploy path**; this is the fallback. |
| `npm run generate-types` | Regenerate `worker-configuration.d.ts`. **Run after any `wrangler.jsonc` change.** |

## Architecture

- **The adapter owns the deploy config.** Edit only the root `wrangler.jsonc`. At build time the adapter generates `dist/client/wrangler.json` (or `dist/server/wrangler.json` once any route is on-demand) and `.wrangler/deploy/config.json` (the pointer `wrangler deploy` follows). Never hand-edit generated files. `name` in `wrangler.jsonc` must equal the Worker's name in the Cloudflare dashboard, or Workers Builds fails.
- **`output: 'static'` + the Cloudflare adapter** — every page prerenders, so the deploy is an assets-only Worker: no script, no bindings. Opt one page into on-demand rendering with `export const prerender = false`. The adapter stays for workerd-based `dev`/`preview`, its auto-injected `/_astro/*` immutable caching, and that one-line opt-in.
- **Sessions are disabled** (`session: false`) — no KV bindings. If sessions are ever needed, remove it; Wrangler auto-provisions the SESSION namespace on deploy.
- **`imageService: 'compile'`** — `<Image>` from `astro:assets` works; images are optimized at build time into content-hashed `/_astro/` files. Chosen over the default `cloudflare-binding` because it needs no `IMAGES` binding and builds faster.
- **Custom 404** — `src/pages/404.astro` builds to `dist/client/404.html`; served with a real 404 status because `wrangler.jsonc` sets `assets.not_found_handling: "404-page"`.
- **CSP** — `security.csp` in `astro.config.mjs` (with `object-src 'none'` and `base-uri 'self'`); Astro hashes bundled scripts and styles and emits the policy as a `<meta>` tag. A meta CSP can't carry `frame-ancestors`, so `X-Frame-Options` stays in `public/_headers`. Inactive in `astro dev` — test with `build` + `preview`. Third-party script hosts (e.g. `https://static.cloudflareinsights.com`) must be listed in `security.csp.scriptDirective.resources`, together with `'self'`. `markdown.syntaxHighlight` is off because Shiki is CSP-incompatible — use `'prism'` if code blocks are added.
- **Security headers** — `public/_headers` (HSTS, `nosniff`, `X-Frame-Options`, `Referrer-Policy`, `Permissions-Policy`, plus a `/_astro/*` immutable fallback). HSTS `preload` is deliberately absent — opt-in only, and removal from the preload list takes months.
- **Fonts** — Astro's built-in Fonts API (`fonts:` config + `<Font />` from `astro:assets`). Do not add `@fontsource`.
- **JSON-LD** — exported as `jsonLd` from `src/data/site.ts`, injected in `Layout.astro`.
- **TypeScript** — `worker-configuration.d.ts` is committed; regenerate after any `wrangler.jsonc` change. `@types/node` matches the `.nvmrc` Node major.

## Conventions

- Every page uses `src/layouts/Layout.astro`.
- **Reusable UI → `src/components/`** (Astro's standard). **Content model:** fixed data (site info, links) lives in typed `as const` modules under `src/data/`; collection content (blog posts, projects) lives in **Astro Content Collections** (`src/content.config.ts`). Editing content means editing a data module or a collection entry — never page markup.
- The site ships with **no opinionated styling** — no baked-in colors, fonts, or layout. `src/styles/global.css` (imported by `Layout.astro`) holds only the universal reset (`box-sizing`, responsive images) and is the home for site-wide CSS; scoped `<style>` blocks for component styles. Styling is a deliberate decision, not inherited.
- Semantic HTML — `<header>`, `<main>`, `<nav>`, `<footer>`, `<article>`, `<section>` over `<div>`. `<main>` and `<footer>` are siblings, never nested.
- **Astro 7 whitespace** — `compressHTML: 'jsx'` strips whitespace between elements on separate lines (`<span>a</span>`⏎`<em>b</em>` renders "ab"). Keep inline text and links on one line, or insert `{" "}`. The compiler also rejects unclosed tags.
- WCAG 2.2 AA — visible `:focus-visible` rings not obscured by sticky UI, text contrast ≥ 4.5:1, touch targets ≥ 24×24 CSS px, the LCP image is never `loading="lazy"`.

## Workflow

- **After editing `wrangler.jsonc`** — run `npm run generate-types`.
- **Before claiming a deploy-ready state** — `npm run verify` must be clean. To check behavior (CSP, headers, 404), `npm run build && npm run preview`, then `npx astro preview stop`.
- **CI/CD** — Cloudflare Workers Builds, not GitHub Actions. A push to `main` goes live within a couple of minutes; PRs and other branches get a Worker Preview (URL posted as a PR comment; `*.workers.dev` previews are `noindex` automatically). A failed build shows a red ✗ on the commit and the previous version stays live — `gh pr checks` or the commit's Workers Builds check run links to the build log.
- **Dependencies** — Dependabot groups `astro`, `@astrojs/*`, `wrangler` and `@cloudflare/*` into one weekly PR; merge it once its Preview build passes. For an Astro major, run `npx @astrojs/upgrade --dry-run` first and follow the upgrade guide; keep dependency bumps in their own commits.
- **Custom domains** — declared in `wrangler.jsonc` `routes` with `workers_dev: true`. A code 100117 DNS conflict needs manual record deletion in the Cloudflare dashboard.
- **Browser/auth steps** — dashboard configuration, and `wrangler login` when `npx wrangler whoami` shows no credential, must be done by the human.

## Knowledge & memory policy

Record project decisions, context, and direction **in this repository** — `CLAUDE.md` (architecture & conventions), `CHANGELOG.md` (what changed), `ROADMAP.md` (what's planned). **Do not save this project's facts to personal Claude memory.** Repo files are visible to the whole team and to every future session; personal memory is not. When you learn something worth keeping, update the relevant file here.

## Accounts & domain

- **GitHub repository:** <github-repo-URL> — auto-deploys to Cloudflare on every push to `main`.
- **Cloudflare account:** hosts the Worker, the custom domain, and Web Analytics.
- **Domain:** <canonical-domain> — registrar: <Cloudflare Registrar / external>.
- **Credentials:** local deploys use `wrangler login` (OAuth) or `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` (takes priority when set). Workers Builds auto-creates its own scoped API token in the Cloudflare dashboard — don't delete it. No secrets live in this repo or in GitHub. Any token created by hand belongs in a gitignored `.env`; account passwords belong in a password manager.

